+// Installment banking: Prism ally a banks its bag B (with `gems` more) now when that costs less than keeping
+// it. The bag is tributed in the end, each gem adding 1/10 turn (x0.67 with a Tribute emblem) to a final channel
+// the win waits on, a round of which is worth the team's whole collection R (team_farm). Under a restart
+// hazard lambda (channel_hazard) a b-turn channel takes C(b) = (e^(lambda b) - 1) / lambda turns, and C is
+// convex, so the bag's share of the final channel is at least C of its own b: R C(b), plus the bag's expected
+// loss with the Prism until then. Banking now costs the
+// trip to the nearest altar and back and the same channel, each round at the Prism's own rate r (rho x its
+// output) worth 1 + p a gem (p its premium, to the win's room), and p on each banked gem its Focus no longer
+// compounds. Read from what every ally reads alike, but for lambda and the carrier hazard, each one's own posterior.
+bool banks_installment(const World& world, const ChampionBelief& a, int gems) {
+    const int bag = team_bag(world, a) + gems;
+    if (bag <= 0) return false;
+    // The bag-independent part, kept per ally while its inputs hold (farm asks group by group).
+    struct Kept {
